<h1>Getting Started</h1>
<p class="subtitle">Install the server, connect an MCP client, and verify what is actually on disk.</p>

<h2 id="requirements">Requirements</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Node.js 22 or newer.</li>
  <li>An MCP client that can launch a stdio server.</li>
  <li>Network access only if you use pack or research tools.</li>
</ul>

<h2 id="install">Install from source</h2>
<div class="code-block"><span class="cmd">git clone https://github.com/penumbraforge/mcp-librarian.git</span>
<span class="cmd">cd mcp-librarian</span>
<span class="cmd">node bin/install.js</span></div>

<p>The installer uses Node built-ins; there is no dependency-install step. It:</p>
<ol>
  <li>Creates the selected home directory, defaulting to <code>~/.mcp-librarian/</code>.</li>
  <li>Creates <code>skills/</code> and <code>keys/</code>.</li>
  <li>Writes <code>keys/private.pem</code> and <code>keys/public.pem</code> with mode <code>0600</code>, unless you keep an existing pair.</li>
  <li>Creates a skeleton <code>manifest.json</code> if one is absent.</li>
  <li>Copies the bundled <code>getting-started.md</code> skill if that filename is absent.</li>
  <li>Detects Claude Code by its CLI and looks for Cursor and Windsurf configuration directories, then asks before configuring any of them.</li>
</ol>

<div class="info-box"><strong>Fresh installs are not empty.</strong> The repository currently bundles one starter skill. The installer does not sign it during installation, so its initial status is normally <code>UNSIGNED</code> despite the generated keypair.</div>

<h2 id="entrypoint">Manual client configuration</h2>
<p>Use the actual repository path to <code>bin/mcp-librarian.js</code>. There is no <code>server.js</code> entrypoint.</p>

<div class="code-block">{
  <span class="kw">"mcpServers"</span>: {
    <span class="kw">"mcp-librarian"</span>: {
      <span class="kw">"command"</span>: <span class="str">"node"</span>,
      <span class="kw">"args"</span>: [<span class="str">"/absolute/path/to/mcp-librarian/bin/mcp-librarian.js"</span>]
    }
  }
}</div>

<p>The installer writes this shape for Cursor and Windsurf. Its Claude Code path invokes:</p>
<div class="code-block"><span class="cmd">claude mcp add mcp-librarian node -- "/absolute/path/to/mcp-librarian/bin/mcp-librarian.js"</span></div>

<h2 id="verify">Verify the connection</h2>
<p>Restart the client, list the tools, then call <code>server_status</code> with no arguments. The handler currently returns this shape:</p>

<div class="code-block">{
  <span class="kw">"version"</span>: <span class="str">"3.0.0"</span>,
  <span class="kw">"skillCount"</span>: <span class="val">1</span>,
  <span class="kw">"indexStats"</span>: {
    <span class="kw">"chunkCount"</span>: <span class="val">4</span>,
    <span class="kw">"uniqueTerms"</span>: <span class="val">72</span>
  },
  <span class="kw">"uptime"</span>: <span class="val">12.34</span>,
  <span class="kw">"config"</span>: {
    <span class="kw">"logLevel"</span>: <span class="str">"info"</span>,
    <span class="kw">"rateLimit"</span>: <span class="val">200</span>,
    <span class="kw">"cacheSize"</span>: <span class="val">100</span>,
    <span class="kw">"skillsRepo"</span>: <span class="str">"penumbraforge/mcp-librarian-skills"</span>
  }
}</div>

<p>The counts above are illustrative because they depend on installed content. Field names and types are not illustrative: uptime is numeric seconds, and the response does not include a home path, signing state, or human-formatted duration.</p>
<div class="warning-box"><strong>Known version mismatch:</strong> package.json is {{ versions.librarian.version }}, while the current initialize and <code>server_status</code> handlers are hardcoded to <code>3.0.0</code>.</div>

<h2 id="first-search">Search and load</h2>
<p>Start by listing the bundled skill or searching it:</p>
<div class="code-block">list_skills({})

find_skill({ <span class="kw">query</span>: <span class="str">"using librarian"</span>, <span class="kw">limit</span>: <span class="val">5</span> })</div>

<p><code>find_skill</code> returns section-level matches. Use the returned <code>skill</code> and <code>section</code> values with:</p>
<div class="code-block">load_section({ <span class="kw">skill</span>: <span class="str">"getting-started"</span>, <span class="kw">section</span>: <span class="str">"available-tools"</span> })</div>

<p>To load the whole file, call:</p>
<div class="code-block">load_skill({ <span class="kw">skill</span>: <span class="str">"getting-started"</span> })</div>

<h2 id="network">Add content deliberately</h2>
<p><code>browse_packs</code> and <code>install_pack</code> use the network. The current public registry lists nine one-skill packs. Read <a href="/librarian/wiki/community-packs/">Community Packs</a> first: same-name skills may be updated, and unsafe files can be rejected while accepted siblings install.</p>
<p><code>research_topic</code> and <code>fetch_page</code> also use the network. Automatic research from <code>find_and_load</code> is disabled by default. Enable it only after reading <a href="/librarian/wiki/auto-research/">Auto-Research</a>.</p>

<h2 id="sign">Create an integrity snapshot</h2>
<p>Run the signing subcommand to sign every flat <code>.md</code> file with the current private key:</p>
<div class="code-block"><span class="cmd">node bin/mcp-librarian.js sign</span></div>
<p>Restart the server so it reloads the new manifest, then call <code>skill_status</code> using the argument name <code>skill</code>. Signing is described in <a href="/librarian/wiki/signing/">Ed25519 Signing</a>; it is not an automatic refusal gate.</p>
